    {
      "text": "Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, Matt. 6:19. Son of man hath not where to lay his head, Matt. 8:20 (Luke 9:58). see the place where the Lord lay, Matt. 28:6 (Mark 16:6). I lay down my life for the sheep, John 10:15. I lay down my life, that I might take it again, John 10:17. Where have ye laid him, John 11:34. I will lay down my life for thy sake, John 13:37. that a man lay down his life for his friends, John 15:13. Who shall lay any thing to the charge of God’s elect, Rom. 8:33. other foundation can no man lay than that is laid, 1 Cor. 3:11. let every one of you lay by him in store, 1 Cor. 16:2. Laying up in store for themselves a good foundation, 1 Tim. 6:19. is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, 2 Tim. 4:8. lay hold upon the hope set before us, Heb. 6:18. because he laid down his life for us, 1 Jn. 3:16.",
